NV method-stream goldens for the NV queue builders
==================================================

Each .expected file is either the dword stream a reference (tinygrad clone
at _tinygrad/, pinned) NVComputeQueue or NVCopyQueue accumulates in its
internal queue (_q) after builder-method calls, or a QMD image dumped as
dwords, driven with the stub device and fixed constants below. No device,
driver, bind() or _submit() is involved: the builders are pure functions
from (device config, call arguments, backed kernarg memory) to dwords, and
these files pin that function.

Unlike the amdqueue goldens, exec writes through memory: it copies the
program's QMD image into the kernarg page and patches it via the CPU view,
and a following exec or signal patches the previous QMD instead of emitting
packets. The harness therefore backs kernarg buffers with anonymous mmap
while their GPU VAs stay fixed fake constants, and dumps the QMD regions as
separate *_qmd*.expected files.

The OCaml generate_actual.ml (lands with the port) must construct the same
two device configs, make the same calls per stream with the same constants,
and print its queue dwords and QMD images in the same format.

Format: one dword per line, lowercase %08x, trailing newline, no headers.

Regenerate:
  uv run python packages/tolk/test/golden/nvqueue/generate_expected.py
Re-running is byte-identical; output depends only on the pinned clone.

Chip configs
------------
The compute/DMA class pairs are what NVKIface.setup_usermode resolves on
each chip; sm_version is what _query_gpu_info reports. sass_version is
derived as in NVDevice.__init__: ((sm_version & 0xf00) >> 4) | (sm_version
& 0xf).

ada (e.g. RTX 4090):
  compute_class=ADA_COMPUTE_A (0xc9c0)   dma_class=AMPERE_DMA_COPY_B (0xc7b5)
  sm_version=0x809 (sm_89) -> sass_version=0x89
  QMD version 3, image size 0x40 dwords (256 bytes)

blackwell (e.g. RTX 5090):
  compute_class=BLACKWELL_COMPUTE_B (0xcec0)  dma_class=BLACKWELL_DMA_COPY_B (0xcab5)
  sm_version=0xa04 (sm_120) -> sass_version=0xa4
  QMD version 5, image size 0x60 dwords (384 bytes)

The QMD version split is compute_class >= BLACKWELL_COMPUTE_A (0xcdc0):
ada is below, BLACKWELL_COMPUTE_B above.

Fixed fake constants (mirror these exactly)
-------------------------------------------
  PROG_ADDR           0x100000    program address (256-byte aligned)
  PROG_SZ             0x1800      program size -> prefetch min(sz>>8, 0x1ff)
  REGS_USAGE          32          register count
  SHMEM_USAGE         0x480       shared memory size (128-byte multiple)
  SLM_PER_THREAD      0x240       dev slm_per_thread (32-byte multiple)
  CONSTBUFS           {0: (0x110000, 0x160), 3: (0x118000, 0x200)}
                                  constbuf index -> (addr, size); addrs
                                  64-byte aligned (v5 stores addr >> 6)
  KERNARG_VA          0x300000    kernarg buffer VA (64-byte aligned)
  KERNARG2_VA         0x301000    second kernarg buffer (chained exec)
  KERNARG_SIZE        0x1000
  SIGNAL_VALUE_ADDR   0x400000    signal value address
  WRITE_VA            0x600000    write32/write64 target buffer
  POLL_VA             0x700000    poll_bit target buffer
  LOCAL_MEM_VA        0x800000    shader local-memory buffer address
  LOCAL_MEM_TPC_BYTES 0x30000     per-TPC local memory bytes
  COPY_SRC_VA         0x10000000
  COPY_DST_VA         0x20000000
  SHARED_MEM_WINDOW   0x729400000000   dev shared_mem_window
  LOCAL_MEM_WINDOW    0x729300000000   dev local_mem_window
  SIGNAL_VALUE        0x100000042 64-bit, pins the hi/lo payload split
  DMA_SIGNAL_VALUE    0x42        the copy signal payload is one dword
  WAIT_VALUE          0x42
  WRITE32_VALUE       0x12345678
  WRITE64_VALUE       0x1122334455667788
  POLL_MASK           0x1
  GLOBAL_SIZE         (4,3,2)
  LOCAL_SIZE          (8,4,1)
  COPY_SMALL          0x1000      one copy packet triple
  COPY_LARGE          2*(1<<31) + 0x400   3 chunks (chunk step is 1<<31)

Streams and what each one pins
------------------------------
Compute (NVComputeQueue), per chip:
  setup_<chip>              setup(compute_class, local_mem_window,
                            shared_mem_window) - the gpfifo-setup shape
  setup_local_mem_<chip>    setup(local_mem=LOCAL_MEM_VA,
                            local_mem_tpc_bytes=LOCAL_MEM_TPC_BYTES) - the
                            slm-growth shape, incl. the trailing 0xff arg
  memory_barrier_<chip>     memory_barrier()
  wait_<chip>               wait(sig, WAIT_VALUE)
  timestamp_<chip>          timestamp(sig) (= signal with value 0)
  signal_no_qmd_<chip>      signal(sig, SIGNAL_VALUE) with no active QMD:
                            semaphore release + non-stall interrupt
  write32_<chip>            write(buf, WRITE32_VALUE)
  write64_<chip>            write(buf, WRITE64_VALUE, b64)
  poll_bit_set_<chip>       poll_bit(buf, POLL_MASK, POLL_MASK) (acq_and)
  poll_bit_clear_<chip>     poll_bit(buf, 0, POLL_MASK) (acq_nor, ~mask)
  exec_<chip>               exec(prog, args@KERNARG_VA, GLOBAL, LOCAL):
                            SEND_PCAS_A + SEND_SIGNALING_PCAS2_B
  exec_qmd_<chip>           the QMD image exec wrote into the kernarg page
                            (program QMD + grid/cta dims + constbuf 0 addr)
  exec_chained_<chip>       exec twice (KERNARG_VA, then KERNARG2_VA); the
                            second exec emits NO packets (stream is
                            identical to exec_<chip>)
  exec_chained_qmd0_<chip>  first QMD after chaining: dependent_qmd0
                            pointer/action/prefetch/enable patched in
  exec_chained_qmd1_<chip>  second QMD (differs from exec_qmd only in the
                            constbuf-0 address, KERNARG2_VA)
  signal_after_exec_<chip>  exec + signal(sig, SIGNAL_VALUE); the signal
                            emits NO packets (stream identical to
                            exec_<chip>)
  signal_after_exec_qmd_<chip>  the QMD with release0 semaphore patched:
                            enable, address, 64-bit payload
  qmd_init_<chip>           the Program-built QMD image for the fixed
                            program descriptor above, before any exec

Copy (NVCopyQueue), per chip:
  dma_setup_<chip>          setup(copy_class=dma_class)
  dma_copy_small_<chip>     copy(dst, src, COPY_SMALL) -> 1 packet triple
  dma_copy_large_<chip>     copy(dst, src, COPY_LARGE) -> 3 triples
                            (2 full 1<<31 chunks + 0x400)
  dma_signal_<chip>         signal(sig, DMA_SIGNAL_VALUE): semaphore A/B/
                            payload + flushing LAUNCH_DMA
  dma_wait_<chip>           wait(sig, WAIT_VALUE) (host semaphore methods,
                            subchannel 0 - shared with compute)
  dma_timestamp_<chip>      timestamp(sig) (= dma signal with value 0)

The wait/timestamp/write/poll_bit/memory_barrier streams are identical
across the two chips (the methods read no device state); both copies exist
to pin exactly that.

Purity contract (what the builders read; the port must need no more)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Device fields: iface.compute_class (QMD version split + setup),
iface.dma_class (dma_setup), pma_enabled (exec; False here, so no
PM_TRIGGER packet - it is profiler state, not builder output),
slm_per_thread, sass_version (program QMD image), shared_mem_window,
local_mem_window (setup).
Program fields (exec): constbufs[0].size (kernarg-page QMD offset =
round_up(size, 256) = 0x200 here), the prebuilt QMD image, dev backref.
Args state (exec): buf VA + backed CPU view, no symbolic binds.
Signal fields: value_addr only.
Buffers: va_addr only (size unread by the emitting paths).
Memory backing: only the two kernarg pages are backed (anonymous mmap);
exec asserts the QMD VA fits in 40 bits.
Env: DEBUG/VIZ/PROFILE/PMA/IOCTL/DEV scrubbed; PMA would enable the
PM_TRIGGER packet, the rest affect imports/profiling only.

The QMD image constructed for qmd_init_* replicates the reference
Program-init block (the qmd dict, smem_cfg, QMD(...) kwargs, and the
constbuf loop) inline in generate_expected.py, specialized to the non-NAK
(CUDA) path. That copy must be re-synced on every _tinygrad pin move; see
the REPLICATED BLOCK comment in the generator.

Skipped / not producible
------------------------
PM_TRIGGER exec prefix: only emitted with profiling enabled (pma_enabled);
  deliberately excluded, the goldens pin the profiling-off stream.
NAK-renderer QMD variant (shader_local_memory_low_size): mesa/NAK path,
  not used by the port's v1; the goldens pin the CUDA path
  (shader_local_memory_high_size).
NVVideoQueue: video decode is out of the port's scope.
Symbolic (UOp) grid sizes and 64-bit dma signal payloads: the copy-queue
  payload register is a single dword; symbolic sizes need the variable
  binding machinery, exercised elsewhere.

Worked example (exec_ada + first QMD deltas)
--------------------------------------------
Method headers are (typ<<28)|(nargs<<16)|(subchannel<<13)|(method>>2) with
typ=2. exec emits SEND_PCAS_A = method 0x2b4 on subchannel 1 with 1 arg:
(2<<28)|(1<<16)|(1<<13)|0xad = 200120ad (file line 1); its argument is the
QMD address >> 8: the QMD sits in the kernarg page at offset
round_up(0x160, 256) = 0x200, so (0x300000+0x200)>>8 = 00003002 (line 2).
Then SEND_SIGNALING_PCAS2_B = method 0x2c0, header 200120b0 (line 3) with
argument 9 (invalidate|schedule, line 4).

In exec_qmd_ada vs qmd_init_ada: dwords 13-15 (1-based) become 00000004
00000003 00000002 (cta_raster_width/height/depth = GLOBAL_SIZE), dword 19
gains 0008 in its upper half and dword 20 becomes 00010004
(cta_thread_dimension0/1/2 = LOCAL_SIZE packed as 16/16/8-bit), and dword
33 changes 00110000 -> 00300000 (constant-buffer-0 address rebased from
CONSTBUFS[0] to the kernarg VA). In signal_no_qmd_ada, the semaphore
payload dwords are 00000042 then 00000001: SIGNAL_VALUE = 0x100000042
split little-endian, pinning the 64-bit path.
